course: dictionary
lesson: 12263
title: Contemporary: modern, and from the same time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Contemporary has two main meanings. The first is modern, belonging to today. «The gallery is showing contemporary art made this year.» The clue is made this year, so contemporary means modern, not old.
explain: The second meaning is about time: existing or happening at the same time as something else. «The school diary is a contemporary record of the 1950s, written while the events were happening.» The clue is written while the events were happening, so the diary comes from that same time.
explain: A contemporary can also be a person who lived at the same time as someone else. «Anna's contemporary, Ben, was born in the same year she was.» Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Contemporary means modern, belonging to the present time, as in «contemporary art» or «contemporary dance».
fact: Contemporary also means existing or happening at the same time as something else.
fact: A contemporary is a person who lived at the same time as someone else.
fact: In history, a contemporary source was written at the time of the events, so it is useful evidence.
fact: The word comes from Latin roots meaning "with time", which helps you remember that it is about the same time.
exercise: «The museum is showing contemporary art this summer.» What does contemporary mean here? | *Modern, of today | Made of wood | Lost and found | Very old
exercise: In history, what is a contemporary source? | A song for dancing | *Written at the time of the events | A map of the modern city | Written by a famous author ten years later
exercise: Ella says contemporary is just another word for old. Why is she wrong? | Contemporary means lost | Contemporary means very old, so she is right | It is the same as ancient | *Contemporary means modern or from the same time, not old
test: «Mo's contemporary, Sam, was born in the same year.» What is a contemporary? | A map of the world | A very old building | A type of dance | *A person who lived at the same time as someone else
test: «The contemporary report describes the battle as it happened.» What does contemporary suggest about the report? | *It was written at the same time as the battle | It is a modern song | It is a dance | It is very old and lost
exam: Which of these is a phrase about modern art? | Curt art | Barely art | *Contemporary art | Ancient art
